1
00:00:11,880 --> 00:00:13,120
True charm

2
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:14,840
is not about pleasing,

3
00:00:16,120 --> 00:00:17,920
but making a man crave you

4
00:00:18,080 --> 00:00:19,400
yet not dare to touch.

5
00:00:22,040 --> 00:00:23,360
When you get home,

6
00:00:23,680 --> 00:00:24,480
use a paper bag

7
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:25,520
to cover your head,

8
00:00:26,080 --> 00:00:27,600
leaving only your eyes exposed.

9
00:00:28,080 --> 00:00:29,120
Stand in front of a mirror,

10
00:00:29,160 --> 00:00:30,040
strip down,

11
00:00:30,040 --> 00:00:31,880
and really take a good look at yourself.

12
00:00:32,640 --> 00:00:34,720
I want you to know very clearly

13
00:00:35,080 --> 00:00:36,120
the most charming part

14
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:37,520
of your body,

15
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:40,200
and then show it without reservation.

16
00:01:25,320 --> 00:01:25,920
Ms. Guan,

17
00:01:26,120 --> 00:01:26,920
here are the contracts

18
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:28,880
with the UK subsidiary from three years ago.

19
00:01:29,400 --> 00:01:29,800
And,

20
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:31,120
here are flowers from Mr. Lin.

21
00:01:31,200 --> 00:01:32,040
He's invited you

22
00:01:32,040 --> 00:01:32,880
to lunch at noon.

23
00:01:33,040 --> 00:01:33,840
Thank you, Mr. Chen.

24
00:01:33,920 --> 00:01:34,600
Put it here.

25
00:01:34,680 --> 00:01:35,360
You're welcome.

26
00:01:35,480 --> 00:01:36,440
I should be thanking you.

27
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:37,520
If it weren't for you,

28
00:01:37,640 --> 00:01:38,520
I would have been framed.

29
00:01:38,520 --> 00:01:38,960
Mr. Guan,

30
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:41,920
we both work for Mr. Lin.

31
00:01:42,160 --> 00:01:43,120
You don't need to be so polite.

32
00:01:43,320 --> 00:01:44,120
I won't bother you then.

33
00:01:44,440 --> 00:01:45,000
You have work to do.

34
00:02:03,360 --> 00:02:04,840
You played a crucial role

35
00:02:05,840 --> 00:02:06,880
in settling this.

36
00:02:15,440 --> 00:02:16,040
So,

37
00:02:19,760 --> 00:02:20,920
what reward do you want?

38
00:02:23,040 --> 00:02:23,960
I hope

39
00:02:24,760 --> 00:02:27,000
you don't forget our promise.

40
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:34,960
Ah.

41
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:41,240
I think we need

42
00:02:42,480 --> 00:02:44,160
a bit more time for the engagement.

43
00:02:45,560 --> 00:02:46,320
Understood.

44
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:49,120
I think Ms. Wen

45
00:02:49,720 --> 00:02:51,560
still has some reservations about me.

46
00:02:58,760 --> 00:03:00,440
Time is the best catalyst.

47
00:03:02,960 --> 00:03:04,160
She'll see your shining points.

48
00:03:04,840 --> 00:03:05,400
Maybe

49
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:06,760
it's just a lack of interaction.

50
00:03:07,160 --> 00:03:07,960
How about

51
00:03:09,160 --> 00:03:10,400
we go back this weekend

52
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:11,560
and have dinner with her?

53
00:03:14,760 --> 00:03:15,640
That's very thoughtful of you.

54
00:03:17,720 --> 00:03:18,400
By the way,

55
00:03:19,120 --> 00:03:20,480
I heard you're looking into

56
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:21,520
the dealings with

57
00:03:21,520 --> 00:03:22,840
our overseas subsidiaries.

58
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:29,560
Yes.

59
00:03:30,160 --> 00:03:31,480
For the company's IPO,

60
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:32,880
I need to thoroughly review

61
00:03:32,920 --> 00:03:34,720
all past contracts

62
00:03:35,080 --> 00:03:36,600
to avoid any historical issues.

63
00:03:36,720 --> 00:03:37,800
Especially overseas,

64
00:03:38,600 --> 00:03:40,440
where issues are most likely to arise.

65
00:03:40,640 --> 00:03:41,400
With you here,

66
00:03:42,160 --> 00:03:42,880
I'm relieved.

67
00:03:45,880 --> 00:03:46,280
Come on.

68
00:03:46,480 --> 00:03:47,120
Cheers.

69
00:03:47,720 --> 00:03:48,400
Cheers.

70
00:03:58,080 --> 00:03:59,800
What do you think Guan Tiantian

71
00:04:00,480 --> 00:04:01,920
wants to do?

72
00:04:03,720 --> 00:04:04,680
Maybe

73
00:04:06,120 --> 00:04:08,000
she just wants to marry a rich man.

74
00:04:09,160 --> 00:04:10,400
It's so real.

75
00:04:11,480 --> 00:04:13,400
This profound pain

76
00:04:14,120 --> 00:04:15,400
is not like an acting.

77
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:17,960
What do you mean?

78
00:04:22,120 --> 00:04:24,120
Look at the things Su Wei sent.

79
00:04:26,480 --> 00:04:27,640
The score of

80
00:04:28,160 --> 00:04:29,320
the lesson of attacking the heart is excellent.

81
00:04:29,640 --> 00:04:30,960
Especially

82
00:04:31,280 --> 00:04:33,120
the sense of brokenness and alienation

83
00:04:33,520 --> 00:04:35,360
is so real.

84
00:04:36,160 --> 00:04:37,560
Even Su Wei thinks

85
00:04:37,640 --> 00:04:39,000
it's not something

86
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:40,920
that can be deliberately imitated by training.

87
00:04:41,440 --> 00:04:43,040
She shows an unusual avoidance

88
00:04:43,160 --> 00:04:43,760
to specific topics,

89
00:04:43,880 --> 00:04:44,680
such as

90
00:04:44,920 --> 00:04:45,680
family,

91
00:04:45,880 --> 00:04:46,720
past,

92
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:49,440
and accidents.

93
00:04:49,440 --> 00:04:50,360
Even

94
00:04:50,360 --> 00:04:51,880
physiological disgust.

95
00:04:52,200 --> 00:04:53,680
A woman with a simple background

96
00:04:53,760 --> 00:04:55,440
who just wants to marry a rich man

97
00:04:55,760 --> 00:04:57,840
wouldn't deliberately cultivate

98
00:04:58,040 --> 00:04:59,680
such a painful charm.

99
00:05:01,720 --> 00:05:02,640
I think

100
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:07,160
she wants more than just to be Mrs. Lin.

101
00:05:07,920 --> 00:05:08,720
It's

102
00:05:08,760 --> 00:05:10,400
something deeper.

103
00:05:15,240 --> 00:05:16,720
Lin Jiming,

104
00:05:18,520 --> 00:05:20,360
the Lin Group,

105
00:05:21,840 --> 00:05:23,120
or

106
00:05:28,360 --> 00:05:31,440
something we almost forgot.

107
00:05:35,040 --> 00:05:35,960
You mean...

108
00:05:36,120 --> 00:05:37,120
Send someone to the UK

109
00:05:37,120 --> 00:05:37,800
to investigate.

110
00:05:38,200 --> 00:05:39,840
Keep a close eye on her.

111
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:41,760
From today on,

112
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:43,480
who she meets,

113
00:05:43,920 --> 00:05:45,160
where she goes,

114
00:05:45,640 --> 00:05:46,440
or

115
00:05:47,920 --> 00:05:50,320
even her subtle expressions,

116
00:05:50,720 --> 00:05:51,720
every move she makes,

117
00:05:52,160 --> 00:05:53,440
must be reported to me.

118
00:05:53,920 --> 00:05:55,680
I need to know every day.

119
00:05:55,880 --> 00:05:56,800
Understood?

120
00:05:58,240 --> 00:05:58,960
Yes.

121
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:08,040
Sir,

122
00:06:08,640 --> 00:06:10,120
this is the case of Niudingshan's divorce.

123
00:06:10,280 --> 00:06:11,840
I've uncovered some new evidence.

124
00:06:11,920 --> 00:06:12,760
Please take a look.

125
00:06:19,360 --> 00:06:20,480
The correlation

126
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:22,000
is not direct enough.

127
00:06:23,320 --> 00:06:24,240
What about Bai Qiang?

128
00:06:24,400 --> 00:06:25,840
She insists it's a marital dispute

129
00:06:26,320 --> 00:06:27,400
and denies any fraud.

130
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:28,720
Jiang,

131
00:06:28,720 --> 00:06:29,520
remember,

132
00:06:30,200 --> 00:06:31,640
evidence and procedure

133
00:06:31,920 --> 00:06:33,920
are our only weapons.

134
00:06:35,440 --> 00:06:36,360
Okay, sir.

135
00:06:36,880 --> 00:06:38,040
I'll keep investigating.

136
00:07:31,840 --> 00:07:32,560
Son,

137
00:07:32,840 --> 00:07:33,920
try this.

138
00:07:34,360 --> 00:07:36,480
The cook made it all afternoon.

139
00:07:36,680 --> 00:07:38,480
It's your favorite since childhood.

140
00:07:39,200 --> 00:07:39,880
Thanks, mom.

141
00:07:49,200 --> 00:07:49,640
Here.

142
00:07:49,640 --> 00:07:50,400
Thank you.

143
00:07:56,800 --> 00:07:57,440
Mom,

144
00:07:58,600 --> 00:08:00,240
Tiantian is actually a good cook.

145
00:08:00,720 --> 00:08:01,920
You can talk about cooking more.

146
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:05,240
You must be busy with work,

147
00:08:05,280 --> 00:08:06,560
so you rarely cook, right?

148
00:08:07,720 --> 00:08:10,160
I don't have time to cook fancy dishes,

149
00:08:10,400 --> 00:08:12,120
but I can make some

150
00:08:12,640 --> 00:08:13,600
simple home-cooked meals.

151
00:08:14,080 --> 00:08:15,560
After all, I'm on my own,

152
00:08:15,680 --> 00:08:17,040
so I need to take care of myself.

153
00:08:17,960 --> 00:08:19,480
I'm quite envious of Jiming.

154
00:08:19,640 --> 00:08:20,360
He can come home

155
00:08:20,360 --> 00:08:22,320
and enjoy such delicious meals anytime.

156
00:08:23,280 --> 00:08:24,560
He's lucky.

157
00:08:25,160 --> 00:08:26,360
But he's

158
00:08:26,400 --> 00:08:27,560
picky about food.

159
00:08:27,760 --> 00:08:28,320
Oh,

160
00:08:28,960 --> 00:08:29,720
really?

161
00:08:29,880 --> 00:08:31,080
So you're picky, huh?

162
00:08:31,400 --> 00:08:32,800
You always seemed

163
00:08:32,800 --> 00:08:34,040
to enjoy the noodles I made.

164
00:08:34,360 --> 00:08:35,280
I thought

165
00:08:35,280 --> 00:08:36,520
you were easy to please.

166
00:08:39,240 --> 00:08:39,840
I...

167
00:08:41,760 --> 00:08:43,480
I was just starving.

168
00:08:44,760 --> 00:08:45,560
And

169
00:08:47,200 --> 00:08:48,080
maybe I

170
00:08:48,320 --> 00:08:49,440
just have a good appetite.

171
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:51,760
What makes a good appetite

172
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:53,120
is not

173
00:08:53,120 --> 00:08:54,040
the food,

174
00:08:54,240 --> 00:08:54,880
but

175
00:08:54,880 --> 00:08:55,880
who you eat with,

176
00:08:55,960 --> 00:08:57,000
and how you feel.

177
00:08:57,120 --> 00:08:58,480
As long as you're in a good mood,

178
00:08:58,480 --> 00:09:00,160
even simple meals

179
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:01,520
can be very satisfying.

180
00:09:04,040 --> 00:09:06,120
You're truly a lawyer.

181
00:09:06,400 --> 00:09:07,120
You always

182
00:09:07,120 --> 00:09:08,680
have a point.

183
00:09:09,280 --> 00:09:10,200
Let's eat.

184
00:09:10,480 --> 00:09:12,080
No talking while eating.

185
00:09:12,280 --> 00:09:13,800
There's always a reason

186
00:09:14,080 --> 00:09:15,400
behind the old rules.

187
00:09:32,640 --> 00:09:33,960
I really like

188
00:09:33,960 --> 00:09:35,280
the gift from Guan.

189
00:09:36,480 --> 00:09:38,160
You know I like sculptures.

190
00:09:38,320 --> 00:09:39,640
That's very thoughtful of you.

191
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:41,720
It's a professional habit.

192
00:09:42,600 --> 00:09:43,560
After all,

193
00:09:43,960 --> 00:09:45,280
knowing yourself and your opponent

194
00:09:45,400 --> 00:09:47,000
is the key to success.

195
00:09:48,280 --> 00:09:49,160
Guan is really

196
00:09:49,160 --> 00:09:50,640
suitable to be a lawyer.

197
00:09:51,120 --> 00:09:51,760
But

198
00:09:51,760 --> 00:09:53,080
in life,

199
00:09:53,280 --> 00:09:54,640
wouldn't that be too exhausting?

200
00:09:55,200 --> 00:09:56,400
Sometimes,

201
00:09:56,600 --> 00:09:58,080
being a bit oblivious

202
00:09:58,280 --> 00:09:59,600
can be easier for a woman.

203
00:10:01,080 --> 00:10:02,160
You're right.

204
00:10:02,680 --> 00:10:03,600
But

205
00:10:04,680 --> 00:10:05,560
I'm just afraid

206
00:10:05,560 --> 00:10:07,040
that if you get used to being oblivious,

207
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:09,600
when it comes to a critical moment,

208
00:10:09,600 --> 00:10:10,600
it's too late to wake up.

209
00:10:11,320 --> 00:10:12,960
It's better to stay awake all the time.

210
00:10:13,640 --> 00:10:14,560
At least,

211
00:10:15,360 --> 00:10:17,160
I can protect the people I want to protect.

212
00:10:17,160 --> 00:10:18,320
Who do you want to protect?

213
00:10:18,320 --> 00:10:20,480
I don't have the ability to protect anyone now.

214
00:10:20,600 --> 00:10:21,360
It's better

215
00:10:21,360 --> 00:10:23,040
to protect myself first.

216
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:42,600
Do you know Su Wei?

217
00:10:48,240 --> 00:10:49,960
Su Wei, the CEO?

218
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:51,720
Yes.

219
00:10:52,840 --> 00:10:54,080
And Mr. Wen?

220
00:10:54,400 --> 00:10:55,160
Yes.

221
00:10:56,680 --> 00:10:57,880
Do you know

222
00:10:58,120 --> 00:10:59,800
Gu Qingyu?

223
00:11:10,600 --> 00:11:11,560
No.

224
00:11:14,320 --> 00:11:15,120
Mom,

225
00:11:19,160 --> 00:11:20,200
what are you talking about?

226
00:11:20,520 --> 00:11:21,320
You look so engaged.

227
00:11:21,840 --> 00:11:22,840
Nothing much.

228
00:11:23,160 --> 00:11:24,240
Just small talk.

229
00:11:24,440 --> 00:11:25,560
It's getting late.

230
00:11:25,800 --> 00:11:26,680
Have the driver

231
00:11:26,680 --> 00:11:27,960
take Guan back.

232
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:29,360
You're not leaving tonight, are you?

233
00:11:30,360 --> 00:11:31,160
Tiantian said

234
00:11:31,360 --> 00:11:32,840
she'll make you breakfast tomorrow morning.

235
00:11:34,400 --> 00:11:35,360
Is that true?

236
00:11:35,360 --> 00:11:36,080
Yes.

237
00:11:36,240 --> 00:11:38,160
I saw you didn't eat much that day,

238
00:11:38,160 --> 00:11:38,960
so I thought

239
00:11:38,960 --> 00:11:40,640
I could change things up for you.

240
00:11:40,920 --> 00:11:41,720
Ah,

241
00:11:42,080 --> 00:11:43,840
that's really thoughtful.

242
00:11:44,120 --> 00:11:44,680
Alright,

243
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:45,720
then,

244
00:11:46,120 --> 00:11:46,720
once you've

245
00:11:46,720 --> 00:11:47,960
settled in with Guan Lu,

246
00:11:47,960 --> 00:11:48,760
come find me.

247
00:11:48,760 --> 00:11:49,840
I need to talk to you.

248
00:11:50,400 --> 00:11:51,000
Okay.

249
00:11:54,440 --> 00:11:55,360
Good night, Mr. Wen.

250
00:12:15,600 --> 00:12:16,120
Mom.

251
00:12:17,280 --> 00:12:17,960
Jiming,

252
00:12:18,840 --> 00:12:19,880
have you really decided

253
00:12:19,880 --> 00:12:21,880
to be with Guan Tiantian?

254
00:12:25,240 --> 00:12:26,160
She's very capable

255
00:12:26,800 --> 00:12:27,600
and can help me

256
00:12:28,200 --> 00:12:29,000
and the Lin Group.

257
00:12:30,640 --> 00:12:31,560
Capable?

258
00:12:32,240 --> 00:12:33,000
Jiming,

259
00:12:33,280 --> 00:12:34,800
you're still too naive.

260
00:12:35,360 --> 00:12:36,600
Her purpose of approaching you

261
00:12:36,840 --> 00:12:37,920
is not simple.

262
00:12:38,160 --> 00:12:38,720
Mom,

263
00:12:39,040 --> 00:12:40,320
I'm not a child anymore.

264
00:12:40,960 --> 00:12:41,920
Can I decide

265
00:12:41,920 --> 00:12:42,800
my own affairs?

266
00:12:42,800 --> 00:12:45,080
I think you are blinded by this woman.

267
00:12:45,160 --> 00:12:46,480
Look at this before you say anything.
